A||N||10||Tina||Compatablity of body panels||||5||
Z||000000||Tina||03-21-2001||11:11 PM||||Kicking the project into high gear,and got a couple questions.<BR>Just bought a 87 T-Top Coupe.<BR>The problem is, I like the looks of the nose and rear-end of my 84 coupe a lot better. <BR>Is it as easy as pulling them of one, and hanging them on the other ?<P>Am I going to run into problems with the molding?( different on each car)<BR>Also,will the 84 decklid fit on the 87 with no problems?<BR>Any other things I got to watch out for?<P>Tina<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hartz||03-21-2001||11:16 PM||||Tina,<P>If you're looking to get rid of the coupe nose and tail, shoot me an e-mail, I might be interested.  I'm just the opposite - I just got an '84 and like the looks of the '87's.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>An '84 decklid should fit any other coupe.  The only reason they changed the decklids in '85+ was to give more clearance for the V6, but I know folks who have put '84 lids on V6's for cooling purposes, and still had plenty of room.  <P>Enjoy your new toy,<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||10
Z||000002||fiero56||03-21-2001||11:17 PM||||I don't have the answer. Just glad to see another bumper pad Fiero fan around <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||03-22-2001||12:10 AM||||The only difference is the moldings.  All the mounting points, etc, are the same.  Might have to swap the honeycomb shock absorber thingy but I'm not too sure about that.  The decklids will swap without a problem.<P>I'd really like the 87 nose if you're not gonna keep it...  I wanna put it on my GT.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||03-22-2001||12:13 AM||||To swap between the 87 and 84 coupe, You just need to swap front and rear plus ALL the trim and parking lights. Mounting points are the same.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tina||03-22-2001||12:49 AM||||Should of known, about the nose I mean.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Not really sure whats gonna happen to it.<BR>If Eric is really going to build the <BR>" sloppiest fiero ever", he is going to need<BR>something for the front end.<BR>But, heh make me an offer I can't refuse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyways, thanks for the info guys.<BR>||||reg||1
