Z||000009||MontanaFiero||03-22-2001||04:33 PM||||the facias should mount the same, but check the alignment position of the marker lamps. Different facias use different positions. I think only the GT/SE facias use the upper lamp mounting, but check for sure.  <P>FYI-- if you ever need to replace door skins, the '84 skins hang on the door, and all the others screw on.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||MrPBody||03-22-2001||07:50 PM||||I swapped the other way, installing an '87 coupe front fascia on my '85 SE.  I changed:<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>fascia (of course) with air dam<BR><LI>impact absorbing "waffle" ('87-88 projects farther forward and is shaped differently)<BR><LI>wheel-well liners ('87 has fatter cheeks)<BR><LI>horizontal "air pan" from fascia to bottom of radiator<BR><LI>marker lights<BR><LI>molding on rest of car<BR></UL><P>Turn signals don't quite align with fascia openings; mounting points inside the radiator air intake are a little different; flexible shrouding in the radiator air channel is different.  But it pretty much all works.<P>||||reg||1
